Z||000006||Gokart||02-27-2000||04:40 AM||||I got a set of scooped aftermarket replacements from <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroowners.com/</A>  that I'm quite happy with. I remember Fierodave selling replacements also not too long ago <A HREF="http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://fierodave.dreamwater.com/</A>  Also try <A HREF="http://www.fieroheaven.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroheaven.com/</A>  They got them too. ||||reg||14
Z||000007||V6pack||02-27-2000||12:26 PM||||I guarantee that a sail panel purchased from the above metioned southwest source will never come off.....<BR>Heck, they don't even crack or wear either.<P>The reason they are so foolproof and you don't have to worry is because they probably won't send you one in the first place....:-))<P>Been there....they done that!||||reg||10
Z||000008||Gokart||02-27-2000||07:43 PM||||V6pack, if your shying around FOCOA you are so right. It kills me to have to not recommend the mother of all Fiero clubs, but they are slow to ship, if at all, and have to be constantly reminded of orders. I'm STILL waiting for vavle stems I was supposed to get over 2 months ago. If it wasn't for that damn good magazine I'd probably drop my membership, but I won't be ordering anymore products from them for sure.||||reg||2
Z||000009||stimpy||02-27-2000||11:44 PM||||Gokart, I think (and correct me if I am wrong V6pack) that he was referring to a place east of FOCOA where Fieros go when they die. (From what I have heard, orders for Fiero parts kinda die there too).  <BR>Can say that the folks down there at Fiero Motorsports (FOCOA) are pretty proud of their stuff and mighty damn condescending. We were trying to get some work done on my dads car by them. Pops was overseas at the time and asked me to make arrangements to get the car in for work. After several phone messages and faxes, I got a very pissy call from Mr. Huff(y) stating that he didn't want to do business with "someone who didn't know what they were talking about". I have NO idea where THAT came from. I don't like to beg someone to take my cash. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||V6pack||02-28-2000||01:36 AM||||Yeah Stimpy, you have it right.  My experience was with that outfit one State east of Ca. where there are a lot of cacti and a big crack in the ground.<P>The wild wild west where Jesse James rode a horse and carried a gun.  Nowadays he would just open a place where all good Fieros go when they die and do the same thing by mail order.<P>My experience was to the tune of about what it costs to buy 61 repro sail panels.<P>And the horse he rode in on!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000011||geyser||02-29-2000||12:17 AM||||Whoaaaaa! I guess I just won't find any sail panels. The one that blew off was an aftermarket one and it was really well made, but I do not know where it  came from. Please o' please, someone out there must have a good reliable source for sail panels. I promise I won't make fun of Ford owners anymore.||||reg||1
